// blaze, the film: under a minute at 60 fps for X, landscape and upright from one scene. A picture, not a deck: every
// beat is a living image drawn by shaders (harness-video's src/backdrop.rs: points of light on near-black, one accent)
// with at most a few words over it, and every number a row of data.json beside this file (harness-video turns it into
// the d_* constants; nothing is typed into a scene, so re-measuring rerenders the film).
//
//   cd crates/harness
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs film.mp4 x-landscape-1080p60       # the film, read back
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs film-tall.mp4 x-portrait-1080x1920 # the same, upright
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs sheet.png contact                  # a frame a second, one image
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs burst.png burst 14.9               # ten frames in a row
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs mix.wav                            # the mix alone
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs sounds                             # every sound event
//
// Storyboard (cuts.flecs has the times; a beat's file has its picture's numbers, its captions and its sound):
//
//   beat  starts  file            picture (shader)                           words on screen
//   1     0.0     hook.flecs      race: three comets, blaze's lands first    "no-op run", the three names and times
//   2     3.8     graph.flecs     graph: a ring from one node lights only    "all cached", "one edit",
//                                 it and its readers                         "only this reruns"
//   3     8.2     core.flecs      core: the daemon, warm, work in orbit      "warm daemon", "sandboxed, byte-identical"
//   4     11.8    swarm.flecs     swarm: a million sparks fall to a few      1,091,174 falling to 21,067,
//                                 (the peak: a rise, ticks, one hit)         "re-verified per edit", "one day"
//   5-8   19.4    noop, body,     beam: a time as a bar of light, falling    the figure and two words each
//                 launch, disk    from its before to its after
//   9-10  31.4    comment, start  race                                       two words, names and times
//   11    38.6    bodyrace.flecs  race: Relax lands first                    "body edit", "Relax leads"
//   12    42.6    cold.flecs      race: blaze still crossing at the end      "cold start", "still behind", "in progress"
//   13    47.3    end.flecs       gather: the points stream in, the mark     the mark, the repository
//                                 forms and catches fire
//
// Honesty (the repository's rule: claims from evidence): a comparison is a measured row of data.json, drawn to scale
// (a lane's time is its share of the row's slowest); the rows blaze loses are shown as they are, and said; "cargo" is
// the stopwatch data.json describes and nothing more is claimed of it; the conditions pass once in the smallest type.
//
// Sound: synthesised by harness-native-blaze's `sound` from the events in the beat files (`harness-video ... sounds`
// lists them), one bed under the whole film, brought to the root's `Mix`. X autoplays muted: the picture carries
// everything, the sound only adds.
include cuts
include tokens
include parts
include hook
include graph
include core
include swarm
include noop
include body
include launch
include disk
include comment
include start
include bodyrace
include cold
include end

@tree ChildOf
film : ui.ZStack {
  Video: {width: 960, height: 540, fps: 60, seconds: $t_out, scale: 2, reframes: true}
  // The picture: which shot and its numbers are cued by each beat's file.
  Backdrop: {shot: 0, at: 0, a: 0, b: 0, c: 0, d: 0, e: 0, f: 0}
  // -16 LUFS integrated, no true peak over -1 dBTP: loud enough on a phone, with headroom for X's re-encode.
  Mix: {lufs: -16, peak: -1}
  Flex: {axis: Z, gap: 0, align: Center, justify: Center, wrap: false}
  Size: {w: {kind: Fixed, value: 960, min: 0, max: 0}, h: {kind: Fixed, value: 540, min: 0, max: 0}}
  // The bed: a low warm chord on A under the whole film (its root at 110 Hz, so a phone's speaker still carries it),
  // and a thud on the first frame's heels, so the hook is heard.
  bed : voice.Pad { Onset: {at: 0}; Lasts: {dur: $t_out}; Pitch: {hz: 110}; Gain: {amp: 0.035} }
  first : voice.Thud { Onset: {at: 0.05}; Gain: {amp: 0.3} }
}
